<h1>Rules and Judging Criteria</h1>
<br><br>

<h3>Rules</h3>

<ul>
  <li>All work must be created during the Ideathon.</li>
  <li>Use of AI tools is permitted unless otherwise specified.</li>
  <li>Teams must submit their pitch deck before the deadline.</li>
  <li>Late submissions will not be judged.</li>
  <li>One presentation per team.</li>
</ul>

<br>

<h3>Deliverables</h3>

<ul>
  <li>PDF pitch deck</li>
  <li>Problem statement</li>
  <li>Prototype</li>
  <li>Video proposed solution</li>
  <li>Basic implementation plan</li>
  <li>Market or impact potential</li>
</ul>
<br> 

<h3>Judging Criteria</h3>

<ul>
  <li>Innovation - Originality and creativity of the idea.</li>
  <li>Feasibility - Can the solution realistically be implemented?</li>
  <li>Impact - Potential to solve a meaningful problem.</li>
  <li>User-Centric Thinking - Understanding of the target audience.</li>
  <li>Business Viability - Scalability and sustainability.</li>
  <li>Presentation Quality - Clarity, storytelling, and persuasion.</li>
</ul>
<br>

